ill gain the knowledge and skills required to analyze and solve complex engineering problems with confidence.  bCITEcElectrical Engineeringh620.1 S132e 2024pT4550500766    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002000032245004200052264002700094520047600121852005900597LAS000023  a978-1-78950-511-51 aDr. David Baker10aElectrical and mechanical engineering 1aLondonbArcturusc2023  aProvides you with all the concepts you need to know to understand the fundamental issues. This book is filled with helpful diagrams, photographs, further readings, and easily digestible features on the development of electrical and mechanical engineering, this book makes getting to grips with the subject as easy as possible. It includes the development of machines and materials, forces and how they are manipulated, gearing, and principles of movement and reliability.  bCITEcElectrical Engineeringh621.3 B167e 2023pT4593000545    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004100031245006700072264003800139520019800177852006000375LAS000024  a978-1-03219332-81 aChristopher Kitcher and A.J. Watkins10aElectrical installation calculations : advanced. Ninth edition 1aLondon; New YorkbRoutledgec2022  aContains all required calculations for anyone who is engaged or intending to engage in a Level 3 electrical course. This would include (but not limited to) both city and guilds and EAL courses.  bCITEcElectrical Engineeringh621.319 K62e 2022pT4535600567    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245004800053264003800101520025700139852006100396LAS000025  a978-1-984688-43-91 aChristian Nollen10aElectrical engineering drawing. 2nd edition 1aNew Yorkb3G E-Learning LLCc2024  aProvides a comprehensive book that examines the visual representation of electrical systems and components. This book involves creating accurate and detailed diagrams, blueprints, and schematics to illustrate the design and layout of electric circuits.  bCITEcElec