izing profit, balance cost and revenues.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh658.5 N111m 2024pT4663800556    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004600031245010900077264003900186520016200225852005900387LAS000032  a978-1-03244528-11 aRobert Stanisławski and Andrzej Szymonik10aSupply chain in reverse logistics : the process approach for sustainability and environmental protection 1aLondon ; New YorkbRoutledgec2024  aProvides a powerful book in which they analyze and present current and future solutions that influence the development of issues in modern reverse logistics.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh658.7 S786s 2024pT4664100570    a2200097   4500001001000000100002300010245005400033264002900087520029900116852005700415LAS0000331 aStephen J. Chapman10aMATLAB programming for engineers. Seventh edition 1aMason, OHbCengagec2025  aTeaches MATLAB as a technical programming language, showing students how to write clean, efficient, and documented programs. This program implements the MATLAB language and provides a very extensive library of pre-defined functions to make technical programming tasks easier and more efficient.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh515 C466m 2025pT4652000561    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002100031245005700052264005500109520022800164852005900392LAS000034  a978-1-39421731-11 aMichael H. Hugos10aEssentials of supply chain management. Fifth edition 1aHoboken, New JerseybJohn Wiley & Sons, Inc.c2024  aDelivers an up-to-date exploration of supply chain operation, explains the issues and problems companies are most likely to face, and presents the solutions and techniques contemporary firms have used to solve those issues.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh658.7 H896e 2024pT4650500651    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002000032245003700052264004900089520034200138852006100480LAS000035  a978-1-77469-740-51 aRushatay Feroze10aManaging change in organisations 1aBurlington, ONbToronto Academic Pressc2024  aProvides an eight-chapter discussion specifically written for students and scholars to meet their needs in terms of knowledge and to provide them with a broad understanding of managing change in organizations. This book also aims to be a resource for academics in many subjects since it will provide clarity and insights for its readers.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh658.406 F367m 2024pT4658100723    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002000031245009500051264003200146520037400178852006100552LAS000036  a978-1-03245582-21 aClaude H. Maley10aEnterprise project management : a comprehensive guide to successful management by projects 1aBoca RatonbCRC Pressc2024  aExplains how enterprises can consistently succeed in managing projects by aligning them with business goals and clearly defining what needs to be achieved. It shows how to ensure that enterprise project management is fully deployed, and that project management concepts, methods, and techniques are available and utilized to deliver business value and realize benefits.  bCITEcIndustrial Engineeringh658.404 M248e 2024pT4663400581    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100005000032245005100082264006900133520020600202852006300408LAS000037  a978-6-214-27193-11 aDr. Marmelo V. Abante and Melchor S. Julianes10aAdvanced production and operations management. 1aManilabUnlimited Books Library Services & Publishing Inc.c2024  aOffers a thorough comprehension of the complexities associated with managing and enhancing business operations in order to address the demands of the current dynamic and competitive business landscape.  bCITEcIndustrial EngineeringhFIL 658.5 A117a 2024pT4632100686    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004000031245009300071264003700164520032200201852005300523LAS000038  a978-1-11985993-21 aR. Kelly Rainer Jr. and Brad Prince10aIntroduction to information systems: supporting and transforming business.