very chapter. The authors draw upon their experiences as working advertising professionals and teachers to get right to the point, stressing key principles and practical information that students and working professionals can use to communicate more effectively to build memorable brands.  bCBEAMcMarketingh659.1 A463a 2020pT4474101324    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004100031245004300072264002300115520102900138852004701167LAS000093  a978-1-47399799-81 aChris Hackley & Rungpaka Amy Hackley10aAdvertising and promotion. 4th edition 1aLondonbSagec2018  aContinues to provide students with a comprehensive insight into the world of advertising and promotional communications. Unique in its approach, the authors situate the key concepts of marketing communications from the perspective of advertising agencies and provide insight into what a career within an ad agency might be like. Their critical approach grounded in up-to-date research allows the reader to develop an interdisciplinary understanding of marketing and advertising, including business, socio-cultural, media studies and consumer culture theory perspectives. Along with striking full colour visual advertisements and illustrations, new examples and case studies, this fifth edition has been fully updated to include: Two brand new chapters on Social Media Advertising and Digital Advertising; Commentary on how the COVID-19 pandemic has and will impact advertising; The evolving role of advertising agencies in the post digital era; Emerging forms of advertising and promotion, including the role of influencers.  bCBEAMcMarketingh659.1 H122a 2018pT4472800576    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002000031245011200051264003500163520022000198852004800418LAS000094  a978-1-29208220-21 aRichard Hammond10aSmart retail : winning ideas and strategies from the most successful retailers in the world. Fourth edition 1aHarlow, EnglandbPearsonc2017  aReveals what the most successful retailers in the world know and how you can apply their secrets to your own business. This book shows you how to use some of the best winning ideas, strategies and tactical thinking.  bCBEAMcMarketingh658.87 H225s 2017pT4473300550    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001700032245008400049264004500133520021300178852004900391LAS000095  a978-1-77469-399-51 aKavita Singh10aSocial media mobile marketing : new age of commercially lucrative relationships 1aBurlington, ONbSociety Publishingc2023  aIntends for students who are interested in commercial, economics, political economy, sociology, and psychology as some to the issues that are discussed in this book may be relevant to social-cultural studies.  bCBEAMcMarketingh658.872 S617s 2023pT4518400650    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002800031245003000059264005400089520033600143852006100479LAS000096  a978-1-11984972-81 aCynthia Snyder Dionisio10aHybrid project management 1aHoboken, New JerseybJohn Wiley & Sons, Incc2023  aOffers practical guidance for combining waterfall and adaptive project management approaches. It also serves as an important guide to hybrid project management methods for project management professionals and academia. It is an invaluable resource for understanding the approach and effectively implementing it for better outcomes.  bCBEAMcManagement Technologyh658.404 D592h 2023pT4474900644    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100006000031245010200091264005100193520022800244852006200472LAS000097  a978-9-81505975-51 aMichael A. Hitt, R. Duane Ireland & Robert E. Hoskisson10aStrategic management : competitiveness and globalization : concepts and cases. Thirteenth edition 1aSingaporebCengage Learning Asia Pte Ltdc2023  aPresents a new, up-to-date standards for explaining the strategic management process and an intellectually rich yet thoroughly practical analysis of strategic management including cases of competitiveness and globalization.  bCBEAMcManagement Technologyh658.4012 H676s 2023pT4487100587    a2200109   4500001001000000020002500010100002800035245006600063264004800129520023300177852006700410LAS000098  a978-9-71235491-5 (.)1 aNorberto A. Orcullo Jr.10aPrinciples of eCommerce/eBusiness : theories and applications 1aSampaloc, ManilabRex Book Store, Incc2009  aCovers some administrative aspects detailing the introduction of computers and electronic commerce movement in the Philippines along with the concept of eGovernment including discussions on the electronic commerce law (RA 8792).  bCBEAMcManagement TechnologyhFIL 658.054678 O64p 2009pT4488000540    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002500032245006700057264003300124520020300157852007000360LAS000099  a978-6-210-44666-11 aJohn Paolo R. Rivera10aStatistical analysis with software applications. First edition 1aManilabRex Book Storec2023  aExpects students will learn and apply statistical concepts and tools to data obtained from various sources that will allow them to formulate assumptions and hypothesis and then critically test them.  bCBEAMcManagement TechnologyhFIL 519.50285554 R621s 2023pT4486200476    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003900032245005300071264006800124520011100192852006300303LAS000100  a978-6-214-27136-81 aFrancis Banaag & Rodolfo L. Ducut.10aInventory management and control. Second edition 1aManilabUnlimited Books Library Services & Publishing Incc2023  aProvides help to those teaching the subject and the students enrolled in inventory management and control.  bCBEAMcManagement TechnologyhFIL 658.7 B212i 2023pT4500500718    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100004700032245005300079264004600132520036900178852006100547LAS000101  a0-324-58053-3 (.)1 aThomas G. Cummings & Christopher G. Worley10aOrganization development and change. 9th edition 1aUSAbSouth-Western Cengage Learningc2009  aProvides students with an excellent grounding in the theoretical underpinnings of the subject as well as describing, in practical terms, how behavioural science can be used to develop organizational strategies, structures and processes. It will enrich students' understanding and study of organization development, change management and human resources management.  bCBEAMcManagement Technologyh658.406 C971o 2009pT4413800549    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003800031245011700069264003400186520015800220852006100378LAS000102  a978-1-29243036-21 aHelen Deresky & Stewart R. Miller10aInternational management : managing across borders and cultures : text and cases. Tenth edition ; Global edition 1aUnited KingdombPearsonc2023  aFocuses on the global strategic positioning, effective cross-cultural understanding and management, and development of effective global management teams.  bCBEAMcManagement Technologyh658.049 D431i 2023pT4517300677    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100005100032245004500083264006800128520030600196852006500502LAS000103  a978-6-214-27135-11 aMarivic Francisco Flores & Rodolfo Lapaz Ducut10aOrganization development. Second edition 1aManilabUnlimited Books Library Services & Publishing Incc2023  aDiscusses the realities and principles of organizational change and its implications within the organization. It also describes the process of implementing organizational changes and the significant role that consultants/practitioners play in addressing the issues concerns emanating from this change.  bCBEAMcManagement TechnologyhFIL 658.406 F634o 2023pT4500200552    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004000031245004400071264003900115520022700154852006100381LAS000104  a978-9-71990568-41 aPerla R. Pereda & Patrick P. Pereda10aPrinciples of management & organization 1aManilabMindshapers Co., Incc2021  aHelps readers to face the world of work with challenges in the organization focusing on discussion about organization, deals with management and leadership as an important component of effective management of organization.  bCBEAMcManagement TechnologyhFIL 658 P434p 2021pT4500801743    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001800031245005500049264003200104520143200136852006501568LAS000105  a978-1-26507040-31 aPaige Baltzan10aBusiness driven information systems. Eight edition 1aNew YorkbMcGraw Hillc2023  aPromotes the belief that technology should support the needs and goals of a business. This perspective is reinforced throughout the pedagogy that presents business initiatives first and how technology supports those initiatives second. Business Driven Information Systems is designed to give students the ability to understand how information technology can be a point of strength for an organization. Recognizing the dynamic nature of information technology, the new 8th edition provides coverage of both current and emerging technologies, in an easy-to-understand format. The clear and concise explanations are brought to life through the numerous case studies, exercises, projects, and questions that support key concepts. The business-driven approach brings the difficult and often intangible MIS concepts to the student's level and applies them using a hands-on approach to reinforce the concepts. McGraw-Hill Connect, an award-winning digital teaching and learning solution, is available for purchase alongside this product. This digital solution empowers students to achieve better outcomes and enables instructors to improve course management efficiency. To complement this edition, the Canadian Companion Connect offers eight Canadian Case Studies and two additional Canadianized modules: (1) Data Analytics and (2) Regulatory Issues. Each module offers accompanying teaching notes and assignable questions in Connect.  bCBEAMcManagement Technologyh658.4038011 B197b 2023pT4512700524    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245009800059264003400157520017100191852005200362LAS000106  a978-1-984680-88-41 a3G E-learning LLC, USA10a3GE collection on business management : advances in business, management and entrepreneurship 1aNew Yorkb3G E-learningc2023  aAims to bring together multidisciplinary knowledge and value creation initiatives from a wide range of business disciplines to address global sustainable development.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiph658 T531t 2023pT4475100525    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001200031245004700043264005400090520021400144852005700358LAS000107  a978-1-11991248-41 aAli Cox10aBusiness analysis for dummies. 2nd edition 1aHoboken, New JerseybJohn Wiley & Sons, Incc2023  aReveals the techniques smart business analysts use to drive better decisions. Get help with brushing up on business basics, identifying important goals, and working with other people to make cool stuff happen.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiph658.4012 C877b 2023pT4474700692    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001700031245011400048264005400162520031100216852005500527LAS000108  a978-1-11987215-31 aClare Murphy10aSustainable leadership : lessons of vision, courage, and grit from the CEOs who dared to build a better world 1aHoboken, New JerseybJohn Wiley & Sons, Incc2022  aShowcases the authors expertise in leadership as he delivers an incisive and comprehensive exploration of how you can reimagine your organization and business model to deliver breakthrough sustainability results which shows that sustainability is not an add-on to business strategy but a business strategy.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiph658.42 M978s 2022pT4474800693    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002300032245004000055264003300095520039700128852005800525LAS000109  a978-6-210-44124-61 aEmerson G. Cabudol10aEconomic development. First edition 1aManilabRex Book Storec2022  aFeatures the theories, evaluating rationalities of the principles to ultimately be used as a basis of policy making, whether in the private or public sector. It also highlights the basic issues of economic development as a precursor to higher economics or policy-making decisions, notwithstanding the interrelationships of local concerns in the economy and the international market. de Avila.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 338.9 C117e 2022pT4483600693    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003200032245002100064264004900085520039300134852005600527LAS000110  a978-1-77469-716-01 aJoao Heitor de Avila Santos10aEntrepreneurship 1aBurlington, ONbToronto Academic Pressc2024  aCaters to a broad spectrum of readers and pedagogical approaches as it offers a holistic view of entrepreneurship, blending academic theory with practical application. Also it covers a wide range of topics, including market analysis, business planning, financing, legal considerations, and more. It also features case studies that bring these concepts to life through real-world examples.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiph658.421 D285e 2024pT4475400619    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003300032245006000065264003300125520029400158852005700452LAS000111  a978-6-210-43888-81 aChristian Eligius A. Jimenez10aManagerial economics in the 21st century. First edition 1aManilabRex Book Storec2022  aGives an overview of how to think like an economist and apply the fundamental business economic concepts and principles, such as demand and supply, elasticity, cost of production, and utility. It delves further into consumer behavior, international economy, and banking in the Philippines.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 338.5 J61m 2022pT4485100486    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245005200059264003300111520017200144852006000316LAS000112  a978-6-210-44376-91 aNorma Dy Lopez-Mariano10aInternational business and trade. First edition 1aManilabRex Book Storec2023  aProvides chapters divided into lessons with their own lesson objectives, lesson summary, key takeaways, formative practice exercises, and connections and applications.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 658.409 L864i 2023pT4484100442    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245003800059264003300097520014100130852006100271LAS000113  a978-6-210-43677-81 aMaria Anita A. Riguera10aManagement science. First edition 1aManilabRex Book Storec2022  aServes as a guide to entrepreneurs and managers in making decisions methodically and help them manage their operations more efficiently.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 658.4033 R572m 2022pT4473400542    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002800032245002800060264006800088520021700156852005900373LAS000114  a978-6-214-27083-51 aAida O. Camilar-Serrano10aEntrepreneurial mindset 1aManilabUnlimited Books Library Services & Publishing Incc2021  aInfluences students to have flexibility of becoming an entrepreneur and to develop their creativity through activities that would make them experience what real new entrepreneurs have done in becoming successful.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 658.84 C183e 2021pT4499300608    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100004300032245003500075264006800110520026000178852006000438LAS000115  a978-6-214-27107-81 aSolita A. Frias & Cristina B. Banastao10aEntrepreneurship. 2022 edition 1aManilabUnlimited Books Library Services & Publishing Incc2022  aPresents an alternative to employment - by being a business owner as it will teach you how to start a business, how to prepare a business plan, how to prepare a feasibility study, how to manage your business and how to interpret your financial statements.  bCBEAMcEntrepreneurshiphFIL 658.421 F897e 2022pT4500000552    a2200097   4500001001000000020001700010245004800027264013000075520019200205852005700397LAS000116  a9-71857228-700aThe Sapat 2000 : integrated farming systems 1aBarangay San Isidro, Calauan, LagunabPhilippine Business for Social Progress - Center for Rural Technology Developmentc2001  aPresents on how CRTD (Center for Rural Technology Development) developed and helped local farmers on how to optimize the use of land with appropriate technologies in their farming system.  bCBEAMcAgribusinesshFIL 630.31369 S187 2001pT4408900504    a2200097   4500001001000000100002400010245004400034264003400078520024400112852005000356LAS0001171 aDr. Asim Chatterjee10aPurposive communication. First edition. 1aNew DelhibVenus Books.c2023  aDevelops your communicative competence and enhances your cultural and intercultural awareness through multimodal tasks. This book was also designed to address the learning needs of students and communicators in today's digital environment.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONh808 C495p 2023pT4496600501    a2200109   4500001001000000020001700010100003200027245006000059264006600119520014900185852005700334LAS000118  a9-71868620-71 aChay Florentino- Hofileña10aNews for sale : the corruption of the Philippine media. 1aManilabPhilippine Center for Investigative Journalism.c1998  aLooks at the history of media corruption in the Philippines, probes corrupt practices in the 1990s and discovers how a free press can be bought.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONhFIL 302.23 F633n 1998pT4430700812    a2200109   4500001001000000020001800010100002100028245008700049264004600136520046700182852005300649LAS000119  a0-07-352615-01 aBaran, Stanley J10aIntroduction to mass communication : media literacy and culture. Eleventh edition. 1aNew York, NYbMcGraw-Hill Educationc2021  aOffers full-semester access to comprehensive, reliable content and learning resources for the Communication course. Connect's deep integration with most learning management systems (LMSs), including Blackboard and Desire2Learn (D2L), offers single sign-on and deep gradebook synchronization. Data from Assignment Results reports synchronize directly with many LMSs, allowing scores to flow automatically from Connect into school-specific gradebooks, if required.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONh302.23 B225i 2021pT4473100538    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100008700032245002900119264004700148520017700195852005600372LAS000120  a978-6-214-51029-01 aFelimon Bonita Blanco, Lito L. Diones, Monique Escalada-Cordova, Janet A. Mananay,10aSpeech and theater arts. 1aQuezon CitybLorimar Publishing Inc.c2022  aProvides a guide for speech and theater arts students to help develop the skills and techniques that will enable them to become more confident speakers and theater artists.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONhFIL 808.5 B641s 2022pT4465300463    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003200031245009400063264004100157520010000198852005500298LAS000121  a978-1-50131854-21 aMichael Ryan, Melissa Lenos10aAn introduction to film analysis : techniques and meaning in narrative film. 2nd edition. 1aNew YorkbBloomsbury Academic.c2020  aProvides students with instruction in how to analyze film images for the meanings they contain.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONh791.4309 R988i 2020pT4472700751    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001400031245007200045264003100117520043700148852005600585LAS000122  a978-1-03228395-11 aRob Cover10aIdentity and digital communication : concepts, theories, practices. 1aOxon, OXbRoutledge.c2023  aExplores the relationship between identity, subjectivity and digital communication, providing a strong starting point for understanding how fast-charging communication technologies, platforms, applications, and practices have an impact on how we perceive ourselves, others, relationships and bodies. It also demonstrates how identity is shaped and understood in the context of significant and ongoing shifts in online communication.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONh302.30285 C873i 2023pT4519400848    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001800031245004800049264003100097520055400128852005600682LAS000123  a978-1-03201774-71 aAlex Richards10aFoundations of data and digital journalism. 1aNew YorkbRoutledge.c2023  aRecognizes a growing need for general data knowledge in newsrooms across the globe, including an understanding of what's possible for both data reporting and presentation and how it can be achieved. It also serves as a roadmap for students and working journalists who seek to understand what data is and how to find it; how to harness it most effectively for news; how to think critically about analysis results, potential shortcomings in the data, and the inclusion of appropriate context; and how to present compelling, data-driven stories online.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONh070.40285 R514f 2023pT4519600630    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245003900059264005100098520031300149852005800462LAS000124  a978-6-219-64880-61 aApolinario J. Lantican10aGuidebook for writers and editors. 1aLos Baños, LagunabDevWrite Publishing.c2021  aEquips the readers with working knowledge about the different aspects of writing. Basic guidelines in simple letter writing, making minutes of meeting, writing research report, and of course, news and feature writing as well as depth reporting in the field of development journalism are thoroughly discussed.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONhFIL 808.027 L296g 2021pT4622300635    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002400032245006400056264005800120520028400178852006300462LAS000125  a978-6-214-48355-61 aNicanor G. Tiongson10aPhilippine theater history and genres : collected essays I. 1aQuezon CitybAteneo De Manila University Press.c2024  aBrings two-part collection of theater essays, putting together the two most important illustrative pieces on the historical development of Philippine theater from its earliest beginnings to 2023 and anthologizes comprehensive essays on the principal genres of Philippine theater.  bCEAScABCOMMUNICATIONhFIL 792.09599 T594p 2024 v.pT4640601039    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100014700032245008200179264005300261520056400314852005100878LAS000126  a978-1-60058-211-01 aSimon Alexander, Grier Cooper, Bill Diller, David Greenberg, Tom Hauck, Melissa LaRose, Matthew Roharik, David Schmidt, Christine Walsh-Newton10aThe daily book of photography : 365 readings that teach, inspire & entertain. 1aIrvine, CAbWalter Foster Publishing, Inc.c2010  aOffers a broad look at life through the camera lens. From brief biographies of world-renowned photographers to techniques in fashion photography and trends, there is something for every reader inside. Packed full of inspiring images and stimulating information, this book is a staple for everyone who loves to point and click. Ten categories of discussion rotate throughout the year: History of Photography, Famous Photographers, Photography 101, Fashion & Beauty, Photojournalism, Nature, Portraits, Social Commentary, Innovations, and Photographic Oddities.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh771 Al374d 2010pT4432600483    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003400031245007000065264003100135520015200166852005500318LAS000127  a978-1-03223131-01 aAleksandar Sasha Dundjerović10aLive digital theatre : interdisciplinary performative pedagogies. 1aOxon, OXbRoutledge.c2023  aExplores the experiences of interdisciplinary performing arts practitioners working on digital performances and in particular live digital theatre.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh792.0233 D914l 2023pT4518800779    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001800032245007300050264004700123520044900170852005000619LAS000128  a978-0-19-285783-51 aAmy E. Elkins10aCrafting feminism from literary modernism to the multimedia present. 1aOxford, OXbOxford University Press.c2022  aDevelops a dynamic study of craft and art-making in modern and contemporary feminist writing. It also expands our sense of trans artistic modernists scholarship to encompass a process-oriented and medium-specific analysis of textile arts, digital design, collage, photography, painting, and sculpture in literary culture. This book interweaves queer research methods and interdisciplinary rigor with a series of surprising archival discoveries.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh820.9 E47 2022pT4520000531    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100006200031245004600093264003100139520020000170852005100370LAS000129  a978-1-03225268-11 aSteve Gibson, Stefan Arisona, Donna Leishman, Atau Tanaka10aLive visuals : history, theory, practice. 1aOxon, OXbRoutledge.c2023  aSurveys the key histories, theories and practice of artists, musicians, filmmakers, designers, architects and technologies that have worked and continue to work with visual material in real time.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh700.9 L785 2023pT4518700519    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003600032245006900068264003100137520018800168852005300356LAS000130  a978-0-367-33752-01 aRafael Jaen, Christopher Sadler10aOff headset : essays on stage management work, life, and career. 1aNew YorkbRoutledge.c2022  aContains essays by a richly diverse group of stage management professionals and educators covering the challenges stage managers face of the job, in their lives, and in their careers.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh792.0232 O32 2022pT4518500532    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001800032245007700050264003100127520021000158852005400368LAS000131  a978-0-367-56824-51 aDerek Johnson10aFrom networks to Netflix : a guide to changing channels. Second edition. 1aNew YorkbRoutledge.c2023  aSurveys the channels, platforms, and programming through which television distribution operates, with a diverse selection of contributors providing thorough explorations of global media industries in flux.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh302.2345 F931 2023pT4519501300    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003000031245008200061264002900143520096600172852005201138LAS000132  a978-1-52972579-71 aMaria dos Santos Lonsdale10aInformation visualisation : from theory, to research, to practice...and back. 1aLos AngelesbSage.c2023  a"In a world of information overload, this book will help you to cut through the noise and communicate information with clear, efficient, and engaging visualisations. Taking you on a journey through a full range of different types of visualisations including infographics and motion graphics, the book: Explains the underlying principles behind information visualisation, including the science of visual perception and cognition; Provides easy-to-digest guidelines that bring research and best practice together; Showcases a range of real-world applied examples, and outlines the do’s and don’ts of different approaches; Shows how to use research methods to design with and for your target audience. From an expert with years of experience researching, teaching, and doing information visualisation, learn how to make better and informed decisions around visualisation design that are appropriate for both your data and audience." -- Publisher's Description.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh006.6 L862i 2023pT4509400539    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001900031245006200050264003100112520023200143852005400375LAS000133  a978-1-03212118-51 aDavid E. Smith10aInnovating the design process : a theatre design journey. 1aNew YorkbRoutledge.c2022  aExplores the process of designing for theatre and details how each part of a designer's own process, no matter what their design specialization, can be innovated and adapter for a more confident journey and for better outcomes.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh792.025 S645i 2022pT4519200779    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001600031245011300047264003300160520042300193852005300616LAS000134  a978-1-03202072-31 aSteve Ahern10aMaking radio and podcasts : a practical guide to working in today's radio and audio industries. 4th edition. 1aOxon, OXbFocal Press.c2022  aGuides anyone who wants to learn how to make successful programmes in the digital era. It examines the key roles in audio and podcasting: announcing, presenting, research, copywriting, producing, marketing, and promotions. It also outlines what is involved in creating different types of programmes: news and current affairs, music, talkback, comedy and features, podcasts, as well as legal and regulatory constraints.  bCEAScMultimedia Artsh791.443 M235 2022pT4518600461    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245002500059264003400084520018600118852004700304LAS000135  a978-1-984680-45-71 a3G E-learning LLC, USA10aPersonal development 1aNew Yorkb3G E-Learningc2023  aDiscusses personal development as a "growth" that is an essential part of a person as it helps to find out opportunity to create a better life mentally, physically and spirituality.  bCEAScPsychologyh155.5 T531p 2023pT4475700941    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003700031245007200068264003900140520060300179852004900782LAS000136  a978-1-46255070-81 aAdam Collins and Jason Harlacher10aEffective bullying prevention : a comprehensive schoolwide approach 1aNew YorkbThe Guilford Pressc2023  aPresents an approach grounded in evidence-based best practices, together with concrete guidance for weaving it sustainability into the fabric of a school as the authors describe a range of ways to support the development of prosocial skills in K-12 students, make data-based decisions to respond to bullying, and build partnerships across student, staff and families. This book also explains how to ensure that bullying prevention efforts are implemented with fidelity and do not fade away over time. An in-depth case study illustrates what effective implementation looks like in the school setting  bCEAScPsychologyh302.343 C712e 2023pT4477200827    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004700031245006800078264003000146520049300176852004800669LAS000137  a978-1-03219342-71 aLinda E. Homeyer and Mary Morrison Bennett10aThe guide to play therapy documentation and parent consultation 1aNew YorkbRoutledgec2023  aGuides play therapists through the case-document process, from the initial inquiry for services through intake session, diagnosis, treatment planning, session notes, and termination summary. It also includes a thorough discussion of ways to structure parent consultations to facilitate the therapeutic process. Expansive appendices provide many cases examples and tips to explain and demonstrate documentation, and the authors provide form templates in the text and on the book's website.  bCEAScPsychologyh616.89 H767g 2023pT4477100401    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001800031245005100049264003200100520011500132852004400247LAS000138  a978-1-26520022-01 aLaura A. King10aThe science of psychology : an appreciate view 1aNew YorkbMcGraw Hillc2023  aEmphasizes the relevance of psychology to the health and well-being of students and the people in their lives.  bCEAScPsychologyh150 K53s 2023pT4476700488    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100004100031245007700072264002900149520015300178852004700331LAS000139  a978-1-11970506-21 aDan P. McAdams and William L. Dunlop10aThe person : a new introduction to personality psychology. Sixth edition 1aHoboken, NJbWileyc2022  aAims to teach personality psychology to any and all readers to engage through conversation and to understand it through a powerful and profound way.  bCEAScPsychologyh155.2 M113p 2022pT4476801065    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100006100032245011300093264003000206520067100236852004800907LAS000140  a978-0-367-53537-71 aGabrielle Wilcox, Frank P. MacMaster and Erica Makarenko10aCognitive neuroscience foundations for school psychologists : brain- behavior relationships in the classroom 1aNew YorkbRoutledgec2023  aProvides a comprehensive overview of brain-behavior relationships relevant to the support of students of all ability levels. Carefully attuned to the shared language between neuroscience, psychology, and education, it covers basic neuroanatomy, brain development in student academic performance, and general assessment and pedagogical implications and interventions in the classroom. School psychologists will be prepared to apply judicious neuroscientific findings to the initial stages of instruction through assessment and intervention, clearly linking best practices for classroom instruction, formative and summative assessment, and evidence-based intervention.  bCEAScPsychologyh370.15 W667c 2023pT4475301297    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001700031245001500048264004600063520103600109852004201145LAS000141  a978-1-53872373-91 aLeVar Burton10aAftermath. 1aNew YorkbGrand Central Publishing.c2022  aIn 2012, the first African American president is assassinated by a white extremist - just four days after he is elected. The horrific tragedy leads to riots, financial collapse, and ultimately, a full-on civil war. In its aftermath, millions are left homeless as famine and disease spread throughout the country. But from Chicago, a mysterious voice cries out...To Leon Crane, a former NASA scientist now struggling to survive on the streets, the pleas he hears remind him of the wife he could not save - and offer him a chance at redemption. To Jacob Fire Cloud, a revered Lakota medicine man, the voice is a sign that the White Buffalo Woman has returned to unite all the races in peace and prosperity. And to little Amy Ladue, the cries are those of her mother, who disappeared during the devastating St. Louis earthquake - and who must still be alive. These three strangers will be drawn together to rescue someone they have never met, a woman who holds the key to a new future for humanity - one remarkably brimming with hope.  bCEAScFictionhFIC B974a 2022pT4532800538    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002000032245007100052264003900123520021800162852004800380LAS000142  a978-0-06-208208-41 aDelaney, Joseph10aGrimalkin the witch assassin. First Greenwillow paperback edition. 1aNew YorkbGreenwillow Books.c2013  aProvides insights into the life of Grimalkin, one of the deadliest witches in the country, if not the world, whose uneasy truce with the Spook's apprentice, Tom, unites them against the ultimate evil of the Fiend.  bCEAScFictionhFIC D337g 2013 bk. 9pT4533700682    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002300032245003600055264003100091520040300122852004700525LAS000143  a978-1-78116-289-71 aPhilip Jose Farmer10aA feast unknown. First edition. 1aLondonbTitan Books.c2012  aLord Grandrith, the fabled jungle lord, is endowed with the gift of eternal life, but with his power comes a gruesome side effect - an abhorrent affliction shared by his nemesis, the formidable Doc Caliban, Legendary man of bronze. Engaged in an epic battle for immortality, the two titans have more in common than they could ever have imagined, but who are the dark manipulators of their destiny?.  bCEAScFictionhFIC F234f 2012 v. 9pT4533601212    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245003000053264002600083520095100109852004201060LAS000144  a978-0-515-15463-41 aChristine Feehan10aAir bound. First edition. 1aNew YorkbJove.c2014  aFor as far back as she can remember, Airiana Ridell has always been aware of her extraordinary gift. She can intuit revealing and illuminating "patterns" in the air around her - whether in a spray of mist, in billowing clouds or in the dense swirls of an impenetrable fog. Her abilities led to her placement in a secret government training facility when she was a child, but everything changed after her mother was murdered. Airiana fled the program, but she couldn't outrun the desperate members of a shadowy cabal who want her, who need her, who will kill to get her. Kidnapped and held aboard a ship bound for dangerous seas, her only chance for rescue is Maxim Prakenskii. He has his reasons for helping her, but he isn't about to reveal them to Airiana. Not yet. Not as the two are drawn together as moth to flame. not when there are so many secrets yet untold that could shatter the quaint community of Sea Haven and all who reside there...  bCEAScFictionhFIC F295a 2014pT4532001166    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245006600053264002600119520086900145852004201014LAS000145  a978-0-515-15612-61 aChristine Feehan10aDark carousel : a Carpathian novel. Jove mass-market edition. 1aNew YorkbJove.c2017  aThe moment Charlotte Vintage walks into his club, Tariq Asenguard's blood is set on fire. The ancient Carpathian had given up hope of finding his lifemate, but now he will do anything to make Charlotte his own. What Tariq doesn't know is that Charlotte is using herself and her best friend as bait - to try to draw out the bloodthristy killers who have already murdered Charlotte's brother and mentor. Charlotte is familiar with Tariq. Not only is he one of the richest and most eligible bachelors in the city, but he's also a renowned collector of old carousel horses, which Charlotte restores. Their shared passion opens Charlotte up to trusting him with her life and with the desire she can no longer control. But it also makes her vulnerable to a centuries-old curse that will unite her and Tariq in a war against the enemies of humans and Carpathians alike...  bCEAScFictionhFIC F295d 2017pT4532100742    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245004300053264002600096520046800122852004200590LAS000146  a978-0-515-14261-71 aChristine Feehan10aDeadly game. Jove mass-market edition. 1aNew YorkbJove.c2007  aIt begins as a mission to protect a politician from an assassination threat. But the operation takes an unexpected turn when Mari, a mysterious beautiful Ghost Walker, is taken hostage. At the same time, Ken Norton, expert assassin and a Ghost Walker warrior, is on a mission of his own - one that reaches into Mari's past. No stranger to the ways of violent warfare, Mari must join forces with ken and trust his every move - each one more intimate than the last.  bCEAScFictionhFIC F295d 2007pT4532201226    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100004400032245003100076264003100107520093600138852004201074LAS000147  a978-1-982192-56-31 aEric Flint , Paula Goodlett , Gorg Huff10a1637 : the coast of chaos. 1aRiverdale, NYbBaen.c2021  aThe fight for the new world is on! In late 1636, the recently formed United States of Europe makes a private pact with the Netherlands. The USE agrees to create no settlements of its own along the coast north of Pamlico Sound (in what is today's North Carolina) and east of the Appalachian Mountains, and it will not contest the Netherlands control of Manhattan Island and the Hudson valley. In exchange, the Netherlands agrees to abolish slaver in its possessions and to assist the USE in suppressing the Atlantic slave trade. But following shortly thereafter, the long dormant French claims to the British territories they purchased in 1633 from the King of England become active, when new French king Gaston sends troops to invade that portion of North America known today as New England. The American Coast of Chaos is set for explosion that may change the future forever - and liberty and justice for all hang in the balance!.  bCEAScFictionhFIC F623n 2021pT4531200965    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003600032245003900068264003100107520067500138852004200813LAS000148  a978-1-982193-02-71 aEric Flint and Robert E. Waters10a1637 : the Transylvanian decision. 1aRiverdale, NYbBaen.c2022  aThe future of Eastern Europe lies in the past. Up-timer Morris Roth and his Grand Army of the sunrise stand at a crossroads. Military success against the Polish-Lithuanian magnates has all but guaranteed a continued push east into Ruthenian lands. There, Roth hopes to further his Anaconda Project so that tens of thousands of Jews are not slaughtered in what's to become knon as the Chmielnicki Pogrom of 1648. But the Prince of Transylvania is thrown into political, social, and religious turmoil as battle lines are drawn. Whatever happens and whoever wins the fight, one thing is certain: the history of Eastern Europe will change radically. In fact, it already has.  bCEAScFictionhFIC F623n 2022pT4531301236    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003000031245002400061264003100085520097300116852003701089LAS000149  a978-1-48148292-91 aEric Flint, David Carrico10aThe span of empire. 1aRiverdale, NYbBaen.c2016  aFighting genocide on a galactic scale. The Ekhat been terrorizing the galaxy for eons, and if the Jao and their human and Lleix partners are going to have a hope of defeating them, they're going to need some help. To that end, Preceptor Ronz, guardian of Earth and greatest living strategist of the Jao, has sent out an exploration fleet under the command of Caitlin Kralik. But after a long search, all the expedition has found are dead worlds. Do they continue to search down the galactic arm in which Earth and the Jao worlds lie, or do they make an astounding leap in another direction? Meanwhile, the Ekhat have a new generation of leaders growing into power who are even more implacable that those who have gone before them. The Ekhat have not forgotten the Jao, nor the damage they have done over the years to the Ekhat purpose. It's up to the Jao-Human-Lleix confederation and the new allies they make to survive the onslaught and turn the tables on the Ekhat.  bCEAScFictionhFIC F623spT4531400621    a2200097   4500001001000000100001700010245004300027264003500070520037400105852004400479LAS0001501 a3G Elearning10aCurriculum design and lesson planning. 1aNew Yorkb3G E-Learning.c2023  aIntroduces readers to a range of theories and approaches to curriculum development, such as competency-based education and outcomes-based education. This book also focuses primarily upon the design and development of curriculum documents that students will develop skills related to instructional design such as the development of lesson plan for teaching and learning.  bCEAScEducationh375 T531c 2023pT4496000460    a2200097   4500001001000000100001700010245004000027264003500067520021400102852004600316LAS0001511 a3G Elearning10aEducation systems around the world. 1aNew Yorkb3G E-Learning.c2023  aProvides information with regards to different kind of approach to educational system around the world to achieve quality education through learning resources, technology, methodology and operation management.  bCEAScEducationh370.9 T531e 2023pT4495800533    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245007800053264003800131520020300169852005100372LAS000152  a978-1-77469-464-01 aKaren Ang-Manaig10aA value-based education for this century : new techniques and approaches. 1aCanadabSociety Publishing.c2023  aExplores the landscape of value-based education as well as the discussions that are placed in the context of communities that have set priorities for educators and the institutions that employ them.  bCEAScEducationhFIL 370.11 A581v 2023pT4496400613    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245019300053264004700246520015900293852005100452LAS000153  a978-6-214-51031-31 aElmer B. De Leon10aLET comprehensive reviewer : based on 2022 enhanced table of specifications (TOS) for the board licensure examination for professional teachers (BLEPT) : specialization : values education. 1aQuezon CitybLorimar Publishing Inc.c2023  aPrepares examinees for the licensure examination providing needed materials of different scope of values education competencies to engage themselves with.  bCEAScEducationhFIL 370.76 D346l 2023pT4497701197    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100006900032245012100101264004600222520077300268852004601041LAS000154  a978-1-83982-795-21 aJose W. Lalas, Heidi Luv Strikwerda, Chris Forlin, Tyrone Howard10aMinding the marginalized students through inclusion, justice, and hope : daring to transform educational inequities. 1aUnited KingdombEmerald Publishing.c2021  aWhile the issue of advancing equity occupies the pages of many education journals across the world and pursuing it in schools and classrooms is a common instructional goal, there is an obvious absence of established school policies combined with pedagogies on how to achieve educational equity. Therefore, equity solution driven by inclusion, justice, and hope is needed to transform the current systemic educational inequities. To ensure and sustain the notion that all children have the opportunities they need to develop, succeed, and meet their potential, it is imperative that we move the discussion about the impact of education from celebrating the academic gain of a few, to the needs of the many marginalized students who are often discounted and dehumanized.  bCEAScEducationh379.26 M663 2021pT4437000559    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002600032245004300058264003800101520026400139852004600403LAS000155  a978-1-77469-110-61 aOscar Alberto Ramirez10aHandbook of education systems in Asia. 1aCanadabSociety Publishing.c2022  aCovers many achievements in the region and the difficulties that still exist in education as it explores various ways to respond to changes, revisiting the teaching framework to improve the quality, and establishing support networks for students and teachers.  bCEAScEducationh370.95 H236 2022pT4495700519    a2200097   4500001001000000100001900010245006700029264006200096520021600158852004700374LAS0001561 aSamuel Robbins10aTheory of modern educational technology and quality education. 1aWilmington, De U.S.A.bAmerican Academic Publisher.c2024  aIntroduces to the readers with the studying and expounding the modern educational technology theory and the university quality education in order to explore the paths and means to cultivate high-quality talents.  bCEAScEducationh371.33 R636t 2024pT4496300562    a2200097   4500001001000000100007700010245004400087264004700131520023400178852005200412LAS0001571 aFilomena T. Dayagbil, Lelani C. Dapat, Remedios C. Bacus, Rivika C. Alda10aThe teaching and assessment of grammar. 1aQuezon CitybLorimar Publishing Inc.c2021  aIntroduces you to the world of teaching and assessment of grammar. It will provide you with enough opportunities that will make you examine the application of the theories and principles in the teaching and assessment of grammar.  bCEAScEducationhFIL 425.071 B131t 2021pT4465700574    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100008400032245005500116264004700171520019300218852005300411LAS000158  a978-6-214-51028-31 aRemedios C. Bacus, Ionell Jay R. Terogo, Roselyn T. Bustos, and Lelani C. Dapat10aThe teaching and assessment of literature studies. 1aQuezon CitybLorimar Publishing Inc.c2022  aIntends to assist would-be English teachers in their journey towards the achievement of outcomes related to the actual teaching and assessment of literature studies in the target language.  bCEAScEducationhFIL 428.0071 B131t 2022pT4465400490    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002700032245004900059264004200108520017300150852005700323LAS000159  a978-6-218-17913-41 aArenas, Chester Dave G10aProfessional development and applied ethics. 1aManilabEDRIC Publishing House.c2021  aTackles the different stages of a person's development process leading to his or her character and personal development to become an effective and efficient individual.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 174.4 A681p 2021pT4441200554    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001700032245005700049264003200106520025200138852005400390LAS000160  a978-1-77469-497-81 aOlga Moreira10aAdvanced techniques for collecting statistical data. 1aCanadabArcler Press.c2023  aIncludes new methodologies based on automatic data collection and analysis systems based on smartphones technology and artificial intelligence, as well as their application in clinical research, sociology, stock market prediction and other fields.  bCEAScGeneral Interesth519.501 A245 2023pT4478300609    a2200109   4500001001000000020001700010100001900027245007300046264007100119520025000190852005900440LAS000161  a9-71868618-51 aSheila Coronel10aPork and other perks : corruption and governance in the Philippines. 1aQuezon CitybPhilippine Center for Investigative Journalism.c1998  aExposes the many facets of corruption in the Philippines and pinpoints who is responsible. But this book goes beyond muckraking to examining the social structures and the institutions that breed graft. It also examines what can be done about it.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 364.1323 P832 1998pT4433600707    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100003500031245006200066264003300128520037900161852005700540LAS000162  a78-6-210-42480-51 aDelos Santos, Danilo Lorenzo S10aGood governance and social responsibility. First edition. 1aManilabRex Book Storec2021  aIntroduces students to corporate social responsibility (CRS) and corporate governance (CG), with theoretical and practical perspectives. Students are made aware of the implications of the effects of business corporation on different stakeholders and the environment, and how these two concepts to organizational success and aid in ensuring long-term business sustainability.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 174.4 D362g 2021pT4475500502    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001700032245005100049264003300100520020500133852005400338LAS000163  a978-0-8294-4170-31 aPope Francis10aThe church of mercy : a vision for the church. 1aChicagobLoyola Press.c2014  aA magnificent book, bursting with profound spiritual insights, from a man who has quickly become one of the greatest spiritual teachers of our time." --James Martin, SJ, author of Jesus: A Pilgrimage.  bCEAScGeneral Interesth252.02 P825c 2014pT4431100474    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100001900031245004400050264008200094520012800176852006000304LAS000164  a978-9-71953525-61 aFidel V. Ramos10aRising to the challenges of leadership. 1aMakati, PhilippinesbRamos Peace and Development Foundation, Inc, 2015.c2015  aShows collection of essays, speeches, and anecdotes of Fidel V. Ramos, former President of the Republic of the Philippines.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 320.9599 R175r 2015pT4431600604    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100007700032245012400109264004000233520013000273852009100403LAS000165  a978-6-210-40092-21 aDanilo M. Te, Divina V. Sabanal, Jovelyn A. Castro, Christopher P. Lelis10aBusiness research with statistical applications : textbook and guidebook for doing and writing research. First edition. 1aManilabRex Book Store, 2019.c2019  aCenters on knowing business research, writing business research and applying the statistical tools for the business research.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 650.0151954 T253b 2019pT44846 T44847 T44848 T44849 T4485000422    a2200109   4500001001000000020001700010100002300027245006200050264005700112520008500169852005800254LAS000166  a9-71913765-71 aCorazon C. Aquino.10aInspiration and images : selected speeches and paintings. 1aMakati CitybBenigno S. Aquino Jr. Foundation.c2002  aPresents selected speeches and painting of the late president Corazon C. Aquino.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 808.85 A657i 2002pT4433200619    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002700031245006800058264005300126520027300179852005700452LAS000167  a978-9-71939852-31 aAsuncion Lopez Bantug.10aLolo Jose : an intimate and illustrated portrait of Jose Rizal. 1aIntramuros, ManilabVibal Foundation, Inc.c2008  aTraces the life story of Jose Rizal as culled from family lore and personal anecdotes. Written by Rizal's grandniece, this biography features the most comprehensive photo album of Rizal, along with the complete bibliography of his visual, literary and political works.  bCEAScGeneral InteresthFIL 959.9 B219l 2008pT4432200540    a2200109   4500001001000000020002100010100002800031245003700059264004100096520023100137852006200368LAS000168  a978-9-71970701-11 aFrancisco Manuel Blanco10aFlora de Filipinas. 5th edition. 1aQuezon CitybVibal Foundation.c2017  aContains information obtained from classic botanical texts and other documented sources. The information in this book is provided purely for education and not as a substitute to any established medical or scientific treatment.  bCEAScSpecial CollectionhSP 581.09599 B641f 2017pT4412800594    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002200032245009000054264004600144520023900190852005500429LAS000169  a978-1-77469-423-71 aDharam Paul Warne10aWarne, D. P. (2023). Business marketing management in a business-to-business context. 1aBurlington, ONbSociety Publishing.c2023  aAims to provide a clear, timely, and engaging examination of corporate marketing management. This volume explores some of the most important factors in B2B relationship marketing and their importance to corporate marketing management.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 658.85 W278b 2023pGS67000938    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002900032245004600061264003800107520062700145852005600772LAS000170  a978-1-77469-466-41 aAimee Concepcion Chavez.10aThe principles of curriculum development. 1aCanadabSociety Publishing.c2023  aAims to provide materials whose specialization or discipline includes a concern for education. More specifically, the book will be particularly relevant for those that are studying education and its related fields. Policy issues and implications that are discussed in this book may be relevant to anyone that is involved in the provision of social services or even social care. This book has been deliberately written in such a way as to appeal to educationists from all walks of life. Once the methodology and values of the curriculum are acquired, it becomes relatively easy to apply them to specific contexts and needs.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 375.001 C512p 2023pGS66600747    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001700032245006900049264003800118520042800156852005300584LAS000171  a978-1-77469-422-01 aSurbhi Jain.10aThe role of human resource management in organizational success. 1aCanadabSociety Publishing.c2023  aAims to those who are generally interested in working people and their experiences in the workplace. This book is useful for undergraduates in a range of management courses. The author tries to locate human resource management within the framework of organizational efficiency while at the same time opening up the department for further scrutiny and appreciation based on its response to the external business environment.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 658.3 J25r 2023pGS66700598    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002200032245002600054264004200080520031500122852005100437LAS000172  a978-1-77469-737-51 aRisha Khandelwal.10aBusiness environment. 1aCanadabToronto Academic Press.c2024  aIntroduces the readers to the basic concepts of the business environment. It sheds light on the natural and technological environment, business and society, business ethics, the foundation of the legal environment of business, labor legislation, the global environment, and industrial and economic development.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 650 K45b 2024pGS66300548    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002200032245005300054264003100107520024600138852005400384LAS000173  a978-1-77469-442-81 aAdele Kuzmiakova.10aThe creation and management of database systems. 1aCanadabArcler Pressc2023  aProvides an overview of the many different aspects of database systems which the content is presented in such a way that even an untrained reader should have no trouble understanding the fundamental ideas behind DBMSs if they read this text.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 005.74 C912 2023pGS66900559    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100003200032245003600064264004200100520025500142852005200397LAS000174  a978-1-77469-729-01 aJohn Ericson A. Policarpio.10aManagement theory and practice. 1aCanadabToronto Academic Press.c2024  aProvides a comprehensive overview of different aspects of management and their importance in organizations as it examines the historical development of each management school of thoughts, its significance, and its limitations on management practices.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 658 P766m 2024pGS66200458    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100002100032245002400053264004200077520017300119852005600292LAS000175  a978-1-77469-756-61 aAbhishek Sharma.10aProject management. 1aCanadabToronto Academic Press.c2024  aProvides broad understanding of project management as it aims to be a resource for academics starting with its fundamentals to central principles of project management.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 658.404 S531p 2024pGS66500619    a2200109   4500001001000000020002200010100001800032245008300050264003800133520028100171852005700452LAS000176  a978-1-77469-394-01 aRicha Tiwari.10aExploring data and business management : how information helps in supervision. 1aCanadabSociety Publishing.c2023  aTakes the readers through several aspects of data management and business management as it sheds light on the several characteristics of data and business management, such as data analysis, big data and business analytics, modern business intelligence (MBI), and data science.  bCEAScGraduate SchoolhGS 658.4038 T623e 2023pGS66800750    a2200109   45000010010000000200021000101000042000